{{!
  Verbatim copy of the typescript-axios `common.mustache` from OpenAPI Generator v7.14.0
  (the version pinned by `openapi:set:version`), with ONE change, backported from
  upstream v7.26.0: `createRequestFunction`'s returned arrow gets an explicit
  `: Promise<R>` annotation and an `as Promise<R>` cast.

  Without it, `npm run type:check` / `build` fail against axios >= 1.19.0 with

    src/api/common.ts: error TS2527: The inferred type of 'createRequestFunction'
    references an inaccessible 'unique symbol' type. A type annotation is necessary.

  axios 1.19.0 changed `AxiosInstance.request` to default `R = AxiosResponseDefault`
  (`typeof axiosResponseDefault`, a NON-exported `unique symbol`) and to return
  `Promise<AxiosResponseResult<T, R, D, P>>`. Inside this generic arrow both `T` and `R`
  are still type parameters, so that conditional type stays deferred and tsc cannot emit
  a declaration for it without naming the inaccessible symbol. Annotating the return type
  removes the need to infer it.

  This replaces the earlier stopgap of capping the dependency at `axios < 1.19.0`, which
  had become a block on 7 high-severity axios advisories all first patched in 1.20.0.

  DELETE THIS TEMPLATE (and `templateDir` from openapi-generator-config.yml, if nothing
  else lives here) once `openapi:set:version` moves to >= 7.26.0, which ships the same
  fix — keeping the override would then silently pin common.ts to the 7.14.0 shape.
}}
